{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788992652401,"sessionID":"ses_f77baaad2ffexBM2MzNFA0qv2Z","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-982098922d855aa5","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/izzyi/.cache/exclurad-mcp-leg-d/2026-09-09-agent-accuracy-opencode-unpriced/aiportal/gpt-oss-120b/baseline/rep1/fx-01/eta/README.md","offset":1,"limit":20},"output":"<path>/Users/izzyi/.cache/exclurad-mcp-leg-d/2026-09-09-agent-accuracy-opencode-unpriced/aiportal/gpt-oss-120b/baseline/rep1/fx-01/eta/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # EXCLURAD\n2: \n3: Fortran code for calculation of QED radiative corrections to exclusive\n4: electroproduction on the nucleon. The current repository contains two\n5: configurations:\n6: \n7: - **Pion electroproduction** (original 2002 code): corrections to the\n8:   unpolarized coincidence cross section and beam spin asymmetry (fifth\n9:   structure function) for ep → e'nπ⁺.\n10: - **η-meson electroproduction** (2025 extension): adapted for ep → e'pη\n11:   using updated EtaMAID-2023 hadronic model tables and CLAS12 kinematics.\n12: \n13: Distinctive features of the underlying formalism:\n14: - Covariant infrared divergence cancellation (Bardin–Shumeiko method),\n15:   giving results independent of the soft/hard photon splitting parameter.\n16: - Exact integration over the bremsstrahlung photon phase space — no\n17:   peaking approximation.\n18: \n19: The code is extendable to any exclusive two-body electroproduction process,\n20: e.g. p(e,e'K)Λ, d(e,e'p)n, ³He(e,e'p)d.\n\n(Showing lines 1-20 of 231. Use offset=21 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# EXCLURAD\n\nFortran code for calculation of QED radiative corrections to exclusive\nelectroproduction on the nucleon. The current repository contains two\nconfigurations:\n\n- **Pion electroproduction** (original 2002 code): corrections to the\n  unpolarized coincidence cross section and beam spin asymmetry (fifth\n  structure function) for ep → e'nπ⁺.\n- **η-meson electroproduction** (2025 extension): adapted for ep → e'pη\n  using updated EtaMAID-2023 hadronic model tables and CLAS12 kinematics.\n\nDistinctive features of the underlying formalism:\n- Covariant infrared divergence cancellation (Bardin–Shumeiko method),\n  giving results independent of the soft/hard photon splitting parameter.\n- Exact integration over the bremsstrahlung photon phase space — no\n  peaking approximation.\n\nThe code is extendable to any exclusive two-body electroproduction process,\ne.g. p(e,e'K)Λ, d(e,e'p)n, ³He(e,e'p)d.","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/izzyi/.cache/exclurad-mcp-leg-d/2026-09-09-agent-accuracy-opencode-unpriced/aiportal/gpt-oss-120b/baseline/rep1/fx-01/eta/README.md","text":"# EXCLURAD\n\nFortran code for calculation of QED radiative corrections to exclusive\nelectroproduction on the nucleon. The current repository contains two\nconfigurations:\n\n- **Pion electroproduction** (original 2002 code): corrections to the\n  unpolarized coincidence cross section and beam spin asymmetry (fifth\n  structure function) for ep → e'nπ⁺.\n- **η-meson electroproduction** (2025 extension): adapted for ep → e'pη\n  using updated EtaMAID-2023 hadronic model tables and CLAS12 kinematics.\n\nDistinctive features of the underlying formalism:\n- Covariant infrared divergence cancellation (Bardin–Shumeiko method),\n  giving results independent of the soft/hard photon splitting parameter.\n- Exact integration over the bremsstrahlung photon phase space — no\n  peaking approximation.\n\nThe code is extendable to any exclusive two-body electroproduction process,\ne.g. p(e,e'K)Λ, d(e,e'p)n, ³He(e,e'p)d.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":20,"totalLines":231,"truncated":true}},"title":"Users/izzyi/.cache/exclurad-mcp-leg-d/2026-09-09-agent-accuracy-opencode-unpriced/aiportal/gpt-oss-120b/baseline/rep1/fx-01/eta/README.md","time":{"start":1788992652386,"end":1788992652394}},"id":"prt_088458395001Z6